---
// Single source of truth for the paste-to-your-agent setup prompt (rendered
// once as the hero below).  Plain text (no backticks) so it survives both the
// copy button's data-code attribute and the visible <code> block.
const AGENT_PROMPT = `Set up Kiln (kiln3d.com) on this computer and connect it to you, then show me it works. I'm not technical: do the technical parts yourself, explain in plain words, and never accept Kiln's Terms for me — only I can (step 3).

1. Install Kiln in its own sandbox (no admin): run  uv tool install kiln3d. If uv isn't installed, install it first with its official one-line installer for my OS, then continue. (uv brings its own Python — don't install Python separately.) The kiln command may not be on your PATH yet; it installs to my user bin folder (commonly ~/.local/bin/kiln; "uv tool list" shows where). Use that full path for every kiln command below.

2. Install OpenSCAD, the engine Kiln designs with — the DEVELOPMENT SNAPSHOT, not the normal version (the normal one is years old and silently breaks designs). macOS: brew install --cask openscad@snapshot. Windows/Linux: get the latest snapshot from https://openscad.org/downloads#snapshots. Confirm it's 2024 or newer. If installing it needs me to click something, walk me through it.

3. Terms: I accept these myself — you must NOT (if you run the accept command, it silently agrees without showing me anything). Paste me the key points from https://kiln3d.com/terms — especially: Free and Pro are for personal use, selling prints needs the Business tier, fulfillment has a fee, no warranty. Then tell me how to open my Terminal and run  <kiln full path> accept-terms  there myself, and wait until I confirm. If I'm away, stop and leave me just that one step. Never use --yes or KILN_ACCEPT_TERMS.

4. Only after I confirm I accepted: run  <kiln full path> install-mcp --force  (the --force means I don't have to create an account), then  <kiln full path> doctor. Note: doctor calls OpenSCAD "optional" and skips its version, so don't rely on it for OpenSCAD — trust your own step-2 check instead.

5. Don't restart or close yourself. As your final message, tell me by name which app to fully quit and reopen so Kiln loads (it's the app I'm chatting with you in), and to open a fresh terminal. Then tell me to come back and type: Kiln, design me a coaster. I should see a 3D preview in a few seconds; if not, I'll paste the error back to you.

Don't run kiln signin during setup (it needs my browser and would stall you). But in your final message, tell me I can run  <kiln full path> signin  any time to create a free account — it saves my designs to the cloud and lets me reopen them on any device — and that it's my choice.`;
---

<div class="install-tabs">
  <!-- Radio inputs at the top level so ~ sibling selector reaches panels -->
  <input type="radio" name="platform" id="tab-macos" class="tab-radio" checked>
  <input type="radio" name="platform" id="tab-linux" class="tab-radio">
  <input type="radio" name="platform" id="tab-windows" class="tab-radio">
  <input type="radio" name="platform" id="tab-wsl" class="tab-radio">

  <div class="agent-hero">
    <h3>Easiest: paste this to your AI agent</h3>
    <p>Have Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, or another AI agent that can run commands on your computer? Paste this &mdash; it does the whole setup for you, on any operating system, with no account needed:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code={AGENT_PROMPT}>Copy</button>
      <code class="agent-prompt-code">{AGENT_PROMPT}</code>
    </div>
    <p class="agent-hero-sub"><strong>Using Claude Desktop?</strong> It can&rsquo;t run commands for you, so this prompt won&rsquo;t install anything &mdash; that&rsquo;s the snag most people hit. Use the manual path below instead: a few copy-paste lines, each one explained. Prefer doing it by hand anyway? Same place &mdash; pick your system.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tab-bar">
    <label for="tab-macos">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M18.71 19.5c-.83 1.24-1.71 2.45-3.05 2.47-1.34.03-1.77-.79-3.29-.79-1.53 0-2 .77-3.27.82-1.31.05-2.3-1.32-3.14-2.53C4.25 17 2.94 12.45 4.7 9.39c.87-1.52 2.43-2.48 4.12-2.51 1.28-.02 2.5.87 3.29.87.78 0 2.26-1.07 3.8-.91.65.03 2.47.26 3.64 1.98-.09.06-2.17 1.28-2.15 3.81.03 3.02 2.65 4.03 2.68 4.04-.03.07-.42 1.44-1.38 2.83M13 3.5c.73-.83 1.94-1.46 2.94-1.5.13 1.17-.34 2.35-1.04 3.19-.69.85-1.83 1.51-2.95 1.42-.15-1.15.41-2.35 1.05-3.11z"/></svg>
      macOS
    </label>
    <label for="tab-linux">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12.5 2C10.8 2 9.4 3.3 9.2 5c-.6.2-1.2.5-1.7.9-.3-.1-.6-.2-.9-.2-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2 0 .3.1.6.2.9C4.3 9.2 4 10.1 4 11c0 3.3 2.7 6 6 6h1c3.3 0 6-2.7 6-6 0-.9-.2-1.8-.7-2.4.1-.3.2-.6.2-.9 0-1.1-.9-2-2-2-.3 0-.6.1-.9.2-.5-.4-1.1-.7-1.7-.9-.2-1.7-1.6-3-3.4-3zm-.5 2c.8 0 1.5.7 1.5 1.5v.5h-3v-.5c0-.8.7-1.5 1.5-1.5zM8 8.5c.6 0 1 .4 1 1s-.4 1-1 1-1-.4-1-1 .4-1 1-1zm5 0c.6 0 1 .4 1 1s-.4 1-1 1-1-.4-1-1 .4-1 1-1zm-4.5 4h4l-2 3-2-3zM8 17v2.5c0 .8.7 1.5 1.5 1.5s1.5-.7 1.5-1.5V17H8zm4 0v2.5c0 .8.7 1.5 1.5 1.5s1.5-.7 1.5-1.5V17h-3z"/></svg>
      Linux
    </label>
    <label for="tab-windows">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M3 5.1 10.4 4v7.5H3zM10.4 12.5V20L3 18.9v-6.4zM11.3 3.9 21 2.5v9h-9.7zM21 12.5v9l-9.7-1.4v-7.6z"/></svg>
      Windows
    </label>
    <label for="tab-wsl">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M0 3.449L9.75 2.1v9.451H0m10.949-9.602L24 0v11.4H10.949M0 12.6h9.75v9.451L0 20.699M10.949 12.6H24V24l-12.9-1.801"/></svg>
      WSL 2
    </label>
  </div>

  <!-- macOS Panel -->
  <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-macos">
    <h3>Install Kiln</h3>
    <p>Recommended: <code>uv</code> &mdash; installs Kiln in its own sandbox, no admin, and brings its own Python (nothing else to set up first):</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="brew install uv&#10;uv tool install kiln3d">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">brew install uv</span>
<span class="cmd">uv tool install kiln3d</span></code>
    </div>
    <p>No Homebrew? Get uv with its one-line installer first: <code>curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh</code></p>

    <p>Prefer <code>pipx</code>? Also isolated, works the same:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="brew install pipx && pipx ensurepath&#10;pipx install kiln3d">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">brew install pipx && pipx ensurepath</span>
<span class="cmd">pipx install kiln3d</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>Install OpenSCAD</h3>
    <p>OpenSCAD is the engine Kiln designs with &mdash; install it once:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="brew install --cask openscad@snapshot">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">brew install --cask openscad@snapshot</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>Install from Source</h3>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git&#10;cd Kiln && pip install -e ./kiln">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git</span>
<span class="cmd">cd Kiln && pip install -e ./kiln</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>One-Line Installer</h3>
    <p>Clones the repo and installs via <code>pipx</code> automatically:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git ~/.kiln/src && ~/.kiln/src/install.sh">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git ~/.kiln/src && ~/.kiln/src/install.sh</span></code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Linux Panel -->
  <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-linux">
    <h3>Install Kiln</h3>
    <p>Recommended: <code>uv</code> &mdash; installs Kiln in its own sandbox, no admin, and brings its own Python (nothing else to set up first):</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh&#10;uv tool install kiln3d">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh</span>
<span class="cmd">uv tool install kiln3d</span></code>
    </div>

    <p>Prefer <code>pipx</code>? Also isolated, works the same:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="sudo apt install pipx && pipx ensurepath&#10;pipx install kiln3d">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="comment"># Debian / Ubuntu (Fedora: sudo dnf install pipx)</span>
<span class="cmd">sudo apt install pipx && pipx ensurepath</span>
<span class="cmd">pipx install kiln3d</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>Install from Source</h3>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git&#10;cd Kiln && pip install -e ./kiln">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git</span>
<span class="cmd">cd Kiln && pip install -e ./kiln</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>One-Line Installer</h3>
    <p>Clones the repo and installs via <code>pipx</code> automatically:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git ~/.kiln/src && ~/.kiln/src/install.sh">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git ~/.kiln/src && ~/.kiln/src/install.sh</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>Install OpenSCAD &amp; a slicer</h3>
    <p>OpenSCAD is the engine Kiln designs with; PrusaSlicer prepares your prints.</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="sudo snap install openscad --edge && sudo apt install prusa-slicer">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="comment"># OpenSCAD (current build) = design engine, PrusaSlicer = slicing for printing</span>
<span class="cmd">sudo snap install openscad --edge && sudo apt install prusa-slicer</span></code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Windows Panel — native Windows, no WSL.  Recommended for
       Windows users with a networked printer: mDNS discovery works
       here but not in WSL 2.  Needs kiln3d >= 1.1.4 (the release
       that fixes the legacy-code-page console crash). -->
  <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-windows">
    <h3>Install Kiln</h3>
    <p>Open <strong>PowerShell</strong> and install <code>uv</code> &mdash; it puts Kiln in its own sandbox and brings its own Python, so there&rsquo;s no separate Python install and no PATH surgery:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="winget install --id=astral-sh.uv -e">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">winget install --id=astral-sh.uv -e</span></code>
    </div>
    <p>Close PowerShell and open it again so it picks up uv. Then:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="uv tool install kiln3d">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">uv tool install kiln3d</span></code>
    </div>
    <p>No winget? Use uv&rsquo;s own installer instead: <code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c "irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 | iex"</code></p>

    <h3>Install OpenSCAD</h3>
    <p>OpenSCAD is the engine Kiln designs with &mdash; install the current build from <code>openscad.org/downloads#snapshots</code> (the development snapshot; the older stable build is slow and has SVG bugs).</p>

    <h3>Connect your AI agent</h3>
    <p>Create your free account (it saves your designs and syncs them across devices), accept Kiln&rsquo;s terms (one time &mdash; it has to be you, not your AI), then wire Kiln into Claude Desktop, Claude Code, or Codex:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="kiln signin&#10;kiln accept-terms&#10;kiln install-mcp">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">kiln signin</span>
<span class="cmd">kiln accept-terms</span>
<span class="cmd">kiln install-mcp</span></code>
    </div>
    <p>Restart your agent afterward, then confirm everything works with <code>kiln doctor</code>. Rather not create an account yet? Use <code>kiln install-mcp --force</code> instead of <code>signin</code> &mdash; local still works, and you can sign in later.</p>

    <div class="wsl-note">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
      <div>
        <strong>You&rsquo;re on the right tab</strong>
        <p>This setup lets Kiln find your 3D printer on your home network by itself &mdash; nothing to look up or type in. The WSL 2 tab next to it is a niche option for advanced Linux setups; if you&rsquo;re not sure you need it, you don&rsquo;t.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WSL 2 Panel -->
  <div class="tab-panel" id="panel-wsl">
    <h3>Install Kiln</h3>
    <p>Inside your WSL 2 Ubuntu terminal &mdash; recommended: <code>uv</code> (no admin, brings its own Python, nothing else to set up first):</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh&#10;uv tool install kiln3d">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh</span>
<span class="cmd">uv tool install kiln3d</span></code>
    </div>

    <p>Prefer <code>pipx</code>? Also isolated, works the same:</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="sudo apt install pipx && pipx ensurepath&#10;pipx install kiln3d">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">sudo apt install pipx && pipx ensurepath</span>
<span class="cmd">pipx install kiln3d</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>Install from Source</h3>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git&#10;cd Kiln && pip install -e ./kiln">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="cmd">git clone https://github.com/codeofaxel/Kiln.git</span>
<span class="cmd">cd Kiln && pip install -e ./kiln</span></code>
    </div>

    <div class="wsl-note">
      <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
      <div>
        <strong>WSL 2 Networking Note</strong>
        <p>mDNS printer discovery (<code>kiln discover</code>) does not work in WSL 2 because of NAT networking. Use your printer's IP address directly instead (works for Ethernet and Wi-Fi LAN setups):</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="kiln auth --name my-printer --host http://192.168.1.x:port --type octoprint --api-key YOUR_KEY">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="comment"># Connect directly by IP address</span>
<span class="cmd">kiln auth --name my-printer --host http://192.168.1.x:port --type octoprint --api-key YOUR_KEY</span></code>
    </div>

    <h3>Install OpenSCAD &amp; a slicer</h3>
    <p>OpenSCAD is the engine Kiln designs with; PrusaSlicer prepares your prints.</p>
    <div class="code-block">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-code="sudo snap install openscad --edge && sudo apt install prusa-slicer">Copy</button>
      <code><span class="comment"># OpenSCAD (current build) = design engine, PrusaSlicer = slicing for printing</span>
<span class="cmd">sudo snap install openscad --edge && sudo apt install prusa-slicer</span></code>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .install-tabs {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .tab-radio {
    position: absolute;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Segmented control — a glass rail with the active platform as a
     filled segment.  Same CSS-only radio mechanism as before. */
  .tab-bar {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 4px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .tab-bar label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 9px 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: color 0.18s ease, background 0.18s ease;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .tab-bar label:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* Highlight active tab label via radio state */
  #tab-macos:checked ~ .tab-bar label[for="tab-macos"],
  #tab-linux:checked ~ .tab-bar label[for="tab-linux"],
  #tab-windows:checked ~ .tab-bar label[for="tab-windows"],
  #tab-wsl:checked ~ .tab-bar label[for="tab-wsl"] {
    color: var(--text);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  }

  .tab-panel {
    display: none;
  }

  /* CSS-only tab switching via radio :checked + general sibling */
  #tab-macos:checked ~ #panel-macos,
  #tab-linux:checked ~ #panel-linux,
  #tab-windows:checked ~ #panel-windows,
  #tab-wsl:checked ~ #panel-wsl {
    display: block;
  }

  .tab-panel h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 28px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .tab-panel h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .tab-panel p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .tab-panel code {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .tab-panel .code-block code {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .wsl-note {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 107, 43, 0.08), rgba(255, 107, 43, 0.03));
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 107, 43, 0.2);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    margin: 20px 0;
  }

  .wsl-note svg {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .wsl-note strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .wsl-note p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .agent-hero {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .agent-hero h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
